# 中频词汇 List03
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025恋练有词
# 描述: 中频词汇List03核心词汇

criterion /kraɪˈtɪəriən/ n. 标准 The main criterion for selection is academic performance. 选拔的主要标准是学业成绩。
curb /kɜːb/ v./n. 抑制；限制 The government took measures to curb inflation. 政府采取措施抑制通货膨胀。
decisive /dɪˈsaɪsɪv/ adj. 决定性的 Her leadership was decisive in the team's success. 她的领导力对团队的成功起了决定性作用。
dedicate /ˈdedɪkeɪt/ v. 致力于 She dedicated her life to helping the poor. 她一生致力于帮助穷人。
default /dɪˈfɔːlt/ n./v. 默认；违约 The system will revert to the default settings. 系统将恢复默认设置。
deficiency /dɪˈfɪʃnsi/ n. 缺乏；不足 There is a deficiency of skilled workers. 缺乏熟练工人。
degrade /dɪˈɡreɪd/ v. 降级；退化 Pollution degrades the quality of water. 污染降低了水质。
delegate /ˈdelɪɡeɪt/ v./n. 委托；代表 A good manager knows how to delegate tasks. 一个好的管理者知道如何委派任务。
demographic /ˌdeməˈɡræfɪk/ adj./n. 人口统计的 The demographic shift has economic implications. 人口结构变化具有经济影响。
denounce /dɪˈnaʊns/ v. 谴责 The government denounced the terrorist attack. 政府谴责了这次恐怖袭击。
deplete /dɪˈpliːt/ v. 耗尽 Overfishing has depleted fish stocks. 过度捕捞耗尽了鱼类资源。
depict /dɪˈpɪkt/ v. 描述；描绘 The painting depicts a rural scene. 这幅画描绘了一个乡村场景。
deploy /dɪˈplɔɪ/ v. 部署；使用 The company deployed new strategies to increase sales. 公司部署了新策略来增加销售。
deprive /dɪˈpraɪv/ v. 剥夺 The war deprived millions of their homes. 战争使数百万人失去了家园。
destiny /ˈdestəni/ n. 命运 We shape our own destiny through our actions. 我们通过行动塑造自己的命运。
detach /dɪˈtætʃ/ v. 分离；脱离 She tried to detach herself from the situation. 她试图让自己脱离这种局面。
deteriorate /dɪˈtɪəriəreɪt/ v. 恶化 His health deteriorated rapidly. 他的健康状况迅速恶化。
deviate /ˈdiːvieɪt/ v. 偏离 The results deviate from the expected pattern. 结果偏离了预期模式。
devote /dɪˈvəʊt/ v. 致力于 He devoted his career to scientific research. 他将职业生涯献给了科学研究。
diagnose /ˈdaɪəɡnəʊz/ v. 诊断 The doctor diagnosed the illness early. 医生及早诊断出了疾病。
differentiate /ˌdɪfəˈrenʃieɪt/ v. 区分 It is important to differentiate between fact and opinion. 区分事实和观点很重要。
dilemma /dɪˈlemə/ n. 困境 The company faces a difficult dilemma. 公司面临一个困难的困境。
diminish /dɪˈmɪnɪʃ/ v. 减少 Nothing can diminish the importance of this discovery. 没有什么能减少这一发现的重要性。
disclose /dɪsˈkləʊz/ v. 揭露 The company refused to disclose its financial records. 公司拒绝披露其财务记录。
discrepancy /dɪˈskrepənsi/ n. 差异 There is a discrepancy between the two reports. 两份报告之间存在差异。
discriminate /dɪˈskrɪmɪneɪt/ v. 区分；歧视 It is illegal to discriminate based on race. 基于种族的歧视是非法的。
displace /dɪsˈpleɪs/ v. 取代；使流离失所 Automation may displace many workers. 自动化可能会取代许多工人。
dispute /dɪˈspjuːt/ n./v. 争论 The dispute was resolved through negotiation. 争端通过谈判解决了。
disrupt /dɪsˈrʌpt/ v. 扰乱 The storm disrupted transportation across the region. 暴风雨扰乱了该地区的交通。
diverse /daɪˈvɜːs/ adj. 多样的 The city has a diverse population. 这座城市人口多样化。
